  "operative_text": "SECTION 1 (Section 23-31-210(5)): 'Concealable weapon' means a firearm having a length of less than twelve inches measured along its greatest dimension that may be carried in a manner that is hidden from public view in normal wear of clothing except when needed for self-defense, defense of others, and the protection of real or personal property or openly on one's person."
